-- title:
--   Definitions for A New Approach to the Representation Thoery of the Symmetric Groups. 2
-- statement:
--   The objects the formalized statements of *A New Approach to the Representation Thoery of the Symmetric Groups. 2* (arXiv:math/0503040) are stated in. Each was checked against the paper by a blind read-back and a moderator.
--
--   - `SymmetricAlgebra`: The actual complex group algebra of S_n (math/0503040v3, pp.8–10). Lean letter i denotes the paper's letter i+1. Multiplication is composition.
--   - `prefixEmbedding`: The first m letters inside n letters; all remaining letters are fixed (p.8).
--   - `prefixInclusion`: The unital group-algebra inclusion fixing the last letters (pp.8–10).
--   - `prefixAlgebra`: The embedded algebra on the first m letters (pp.8–10).
--   - `prefixCenter`: The image of the center of C[S_m], rather than the center of C[S_n] (p.10).
--   - `gzAlgebra`: The source GZ algebra: generated by embedded level centers, independently of all claims about its eigenvectors or generators (p.7). Including level 0 adds only scalars to the unital algebra.
--   - `swapAlgebraElement`: Individual transpositions, each included once in a YJM sum (p.10).
--   - `yjm`: X_(i+1) = sum over j<i of (j+1,i+1); in particular X_1=0 (p.10).
--   - `Adjacent`: Valid adjacent positions, excluding an accidental last-position truncation (p.14).
--   - `nextPosition`: The next position, with its genuine range proof (p.14).
--   - `adjacentPerm`: The adjacent Coxeter permutation s_(i+1) (p.14).
--   - `adjacentElement`: Its actual element of the group algebra (p.14).
--   - `IsCommutativeSubalgebra`: Commutativity of a specified subalgebra, expressed in the ambient algebra (p.8).
--   - `IsIrreducibleAlgebra`: Nonzero simple finite-dimensional algebra representations (pp.6–8). Using all coordinate dimensions avoids an assumed shape classification.
--   - `intertwiningSpace`: The actual equivariant Hom space. Its finite complex dimension is the source restriction multiplicity (pp.6,8). rho is the target action.
--   - `HasSimpleRestriction`: Simple restriction multiplicities: dimension of each actual Hom is at most one, for every pair of irreducibles (p.8).
--   - `IsRealForm`: A real form means a multiplicatively closed real subalgebra whose unique complexification is A: x=a+ib, a,b in R (p.9).
--   - `IsWeightVector`: Genuine joint eigenvectors of the actual YJM actions; no tableau definition is used to define the spectrum (p.13). Vectors are nonzero, and their scale is free.
--   - `spectrum`: Spectrum across all finite-dimensional nonzero irreducibles (p.13). This is independent of content vectors and of Young diagrams.
--   - `SameIrreducible`: Source relation alpha~beta: the two weights occur in the same irreducible module (p.13), independently of admissible swaps.
--   - `contentVectors`: Three independent content-vector conditions, including integer entries (pp.17–19). At n=0 they are vacuous.
--   - `AdmissibleStep`: A single source-admissible swap (pp.17,19).
--   - `AdmissiblyEquivalent`: Finite reachability by admissible swaps; never defined by endpoints (p.19).
--   - `YoungTableau`: An ordinary tableau records each successively added box. Every prefix is a finite lower ideal, so this is exactly a path in the Young graph (pp.19–20).
--   - `tableauShape`: The endpoint diagram of the path (p.20).
--   - `boxContent`: Content is column minus row in Mathlib's matrix coordinates (p.20).
--   - `tableauContent`: The content vector computed from the actual boxes, not from a spectrum or an existence choice (p.20).
--   - `TableauStep`: A tableau swap exchanges adjacent labels in different rows and columns (p.20). All intermediate tableaux remain actual paths.
--   - `labelAt`: Lookup of a box's zero-based label in a tableau. Used only on boxes of that tableau in inversion counts (p.21).
--   - `inversionsBetween`: The source inversion number of the relabelling from T to U, for equal endpoints; this is not an infimum with a default value (p.21).
--   - `YoungEdge`: The Young graph's actual one-box edges, independently of lattice covers (p.20; p.25).
--   - `deleteLast`: Deleting the last symbol from its cycle, keeping all other letters. removeNone redirects the arrow into the deleted letter to its successor (p.25).
--   - `deletionLinear`: The linear extension of deletion, not an algebra homomorphism (p.25).
--   - `tailEmbedding`: Embedding the last k letters of S_(n+k), with no rebasing of ambient YJM elements (p.26).
--   - `tailElement`: An individual element of the tail S_k inside the ambient algebra (p.26).
--   - `IsFullCycle`: Transitivity on all n letters: precisely a full n-cycle when n≥1, including the identity for n=1 (p.28).
--   - `HeckeFree`: Free generators Y_1,...,Y_n and s_1,...,s_(n-1) (p.15).
--   - `freeY`: Free Y generator (p.15).
--   - `freeS`: Free Coxeter generator (p.15).
--   - `HeckeRelations`: The exact degenerate affine Hecke relations: commuting Y's, Coxeter involutions with braid and distant relations, and s_i Y_i+1=Y_(i+1) s_i where the added 1 is the algebra identity (pp.14–15).
--   - `Hecke`: The presented algebra H(n); this definition does not identify it with its finite-dimensional group-algebra image (p.15).
--   - `heckeY`: Canonical presented Y generator (p.15).
--   - `heckeS`: Canonical presented s generator (p.15).
--   - `KillFirst`: Relation killing Y_1. At n=0 the relation is empty (p.15).
--   - `hermitianPair`: Hermitian pairing in coordinates, conjugate-linear in the first input (pp.6–7). It is not the default Pi norm.
--   - `InvariantHermitian`: The chosen positive definite invariant Hermitian inner product of p.7. Keeping its Gram matrix explicit avoids treating the Pi norm as invariant.
--   - `IrreducibleRepresentative`: A concrete coordinate representative of an irreducible S_n-module (p.6). The zero representation is excluded by IsIrreducibleAlgebra.
--   - `EquivalentRepresentatives`: Actual equivalence of complex representations, not equality of dimensions or coincidence of a selected eigenvalue (p.6).
--   - `IrreducibleClass`: A set-sized skeleton: genuine equivalence classes of all irreducibles, constructed independently of Young diagrams (p.6).
--   - `classRepresentative`: A representative of a genuine equivalence class; no desired spectral or branching property is used to choose it (pp.6–7).
--   - `branchingMultiplicity`: Actual adjacent restriction multiplicity between irreducible classes (p.6).
--   - `BranchingPath`: Paths in the actual branching graph, independently of tableaux (pp.6–7). At level zero the irreducible of the scalar algebra is the trivial vertex.
--   - `BranchingPathsToClass`: Paths ending at the specified actual irreducible class (p.7).
--   - `restrictedIsotypic`: The C-isotypic subspace of a restricted target module is the sum of ranges of all actual equivariant maps from C (p.7). Submodule suprema are genuine sums of subspaces, with no unbounded-real default convention.
--   - `canonicalLine`: The canonical path subspace: intersect the independently constructed isotypic subspaces along the path (p.7). No line dimension, decomposition, eigenbasis or diagonal-algebra equality is assumed in this definition.
--   - `ClassHasWeight`: Actual weights in a particular class, independent of the diagram label and all admissible-swap relations (p.13).
--   - `PathHasWeight`: A path's weight has the prescribed prefix weight in each actual vertex representation (pp.7,13). This avoids choosing eigenvalues by a default value.
--   - `IsMaximalCommutative`: Genuine maximal commutativity, including ambient containment, rather than commutativity alone (pp.8,13).
-- source:
--   A New Approach to the Representation Thoery of the Symmetric Groups. 2, arXiv:math/0503040v3, https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0503040v3

import Mathlib

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Renew46.P26

open scoped BigOperators

attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable

/-- The actual complex group algebra of S_n (math/0503040v3, pp.8–10).
Lean letter i denotes the paper's letter i+1. Multiplication is composition. -/
abbrev SymmetricAlgebra (n : ℕ) := MonoidAlgebra ℂ (Equiv.Perm (Fin n))

/-- The first m letters inside n letters; all remaining letters are fixed (p.8). -/
def prefixEmbedding {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) : Fin m ↪ Fin n where
  toFun i := ⟨i.val, lt_of_lt_of_le i.isLt h⟩
  inj' := by
    intro i j hij
    apply Fin.ext
    exact congrArg (fun x : Fin n => x.val) hij

/-- The unital group-algebra inclusion fixing the last letters (pp.8–10). -/
def prefixInclusion {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) :
    SymmetricAlgebra m →ₐ[ℂ] SymmetricAlgebra n :=
  MonoidAlgebra.mapDomainAlgHom ℂ ℂ
    (Equiv.Perm.viaEmbeddingHom (prefixEmbedding h))

/-- The embedded algebra on the first m letters (pp.8–10). -/
def prefixAlgebra {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) : Subalgebra ℂ (SymmetricAlgebra n) :=
  (prefixInclusion h).range

/-- The image of the center of C[S_m], rather than the center of C[S_n] (p.10). -/
def prefixCenter {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) : Subalgebra ℂ (SymmetricAlgebra n) :=
  (Subalgebra.center ℂ (SymmetricAlgebra m)).map (prefixInclusion h)

/-- The source GZ algebra: generated by embedded level centers, independently
of all claims about its eigenvectors or generators (p.7). Including level 0 adds
only scalars to the unital algebra. -/
def gzAlgebra (n : ℕ) : Subalgebra ℂ (SymmetricAlgebra n) :=
  Algebra.adjoin ℂ {a | ∃ m, ∃ h : m ≤ n, a ∈ prefixCenter h}

/-- Individual transpositions, each included once in a YJM sum (p.10). -/
def swapAlgebraElement {n : ℕ} (i j : Fin n) : SymmetricAlgebra n :=
  MonoidAlgebra.single (Equiv.swap i j) 1

/-- X_(i+1) = sum over j<i of (j+1,i+1); in particular X_1=0 (p.10). -/
def yjm {n : ℕ} (i : Fin n) : SymmetricAlgebra n :=
  ∑ j ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun j : Fin n => j < i), swapAlgebraElement j i

/-- Valid adjacent positions, excluding an accidental last-position truncation (p.14). -/
abbrev Adjacent (n : ℕ) := {i : Fin n // i.val + 1 < n}

/-- The next position, with its genuine range proof (p.14). -/
def nextPosition {n : ℕ} (i : Adjacent n) : Fin n := ⟨i.val.val + 1, i.property⟩

/-- The adjacent Coxeter permutation s_(i+1) (p.14). -/
def adjacentPerm {n : ℕ} (i : Adjacent n) : Equiv.Perm (Fin n) :=
  Equiv.swap i.val (nextPosition i)

/-- Its actual element of the group algebra (p.14). -/
def adjacentElement {n : ℕ} (i : Adjacent n) : SymmetricAlgebra n :=
  MonoidAlgebra.single (adjacentPerm i) 1

/-- Commutativity of a specified subalgebra, expressed in the ambient algebra (p.8). -/
def IsCommutativeSubalgebra {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A]
    (B : Subalgebra ℂ A) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ B, ∀ y ∈ B, x * y = y * x

/-- Nonzero simple finite-dimensional algebra representations (pp.6–8).
Using all coordinate dimensions avoids an assumed shape classification. -/
def IsIrreducibleAlgebra {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A] {d : ℕ}
    (rho : A →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ)) : Prop :=
  0 < d ∧ ∀ U : Submodule ℂ (Fin d → ℂ),
    (∀ a v, v ∈ U → rho a v ∈ U) → U = ⊥ ∨ U = ⊤

/-- The actual equivariant Hom space. Its finite complex dimension is the
source restriction multiplicity (pp.6,8). rho is the target action. -/
def intertwiningSpace {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A] {d e : ℕ}
    (rho : A →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ))
    (sigma : A →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin e → ℂ)) :
    Submodule ℂ ((Fin e → ℂ) →ₗ[ℂ] (Fin d → ℂ)) where
  carrier := {f | ∀ a v, f (sigma a v) = rho a (f v)}
  zero_mem' := by simp
  add_mem' := by
    intro f g hf hg a v
    simp only [LinearMap.add_apply, map_add, hf a v, hg a v]
  smul_mem' := by
    intro c f hf a v
    simp only [LinearMap.smul_apply, map_smul, hf a v]

/-- Simple restriction multiplicities: dimension of each actual Hom is at most
one, for every pair of irreducibles (p.8). -/
def HasSimpleRestriction {A B : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A]
    [Ring B] [Algebra ℂ B] (f : B →ₐ[ℂ] A) : Prop :=
  ∀ d e, ∀ rho : A →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ),
    ∀ sigma : B →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin e → ℂ),
      IsIrreducibleAlgebra rho → IsIrreducibleAlgebra sigma →
      Module.finrank ℂ (intertwiningSpace (rho.comp f) sigma) ≤ 1

/-- A real form means a multiplicatively closed real subalgebra whose unique
complexification is A: x=a+ib, a,b in R (p.9). -/
def IsRealForm {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A] [Algebra ℝ A] [IsScalarTower ℝ ℂ A] (R : Subalgebra ℝ A) : Prop :=
  Function.Bijective (fun p : R × R => (p.1 : A) + Complex.I • (p.2 : A))

/-- Genuine joint eigenvectors of the actual YJM actions; no tableau definition
is used to define the spectrum (p.13). Vectors are nonzero, and their scale is free. -/
def IsWeightVector {n d : ℕ}
    (rho : SymmetricAlgebra n →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ))
    (alpha : Fin n → ℂ) (v : Fin d → ℂ) : Prop :=
  v ≠ 0 ∧ ∀ i, rho (yjm i) v = alpha i • v

/-- Spectrum across all finite-dimensional nonzero irreducibles (p.13).
This is independent of content vectors and of Young diagrams. -/
def spectrum (n : ℕ) : Set (Fin n → ℂ) :=
  {alpha | ∃ d, ∃ rho : SymmetricAlgebra n →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ),
    IsIrreducibleAlgebra rho ∧ ∃ v, IsWeightVector rho alpha v}

/-- Source relation alpha~beta: the two weights occur in the same irreducible
module (p.13), independently of admissible swaps. -/
def SameIrreducible {n : ℕ} (alpha beta : Fin n → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ d, ∃ rho : SymmetricAlgebra n →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ),
    IsIrreducibleAlgebra rho ∧ ∃ v w,
      IsWeightVector rho alpha v ∧ IsWeightVector rho beta w

/-- Three independent content-vector conditions, including integer entries
(pp.17–19). At n=0 they are vacuous. -/
def contentVectors (n : ℕ) : Set (Fin n → ℂ) :=
  {alpha | (∀ i, ∃ z : ℤ, alpha i = (z : ℂ)) ∧
    (∀ i : Fin n, i.val = 0 → alpha i = 0) ∧
    (∀ q : Fin n, 0 < q.val → ∃ p : Fin n, p < q ∧
      (alpha p = alpha q - 1 ∨ alpha p = alpha q + 1)) ∧
    (∀ p q : Fin n, p < q → alpha p = alpha q →
      (∃ r : Fin n, p < r ∧ r < q ∧ alpha r = alpha p - 1) ∧
      (∃ r : Fin n, p < r ∧ r < q ∧ alpha r = alpha p + 1))}

/-- A single source-admissible swap (pp.17,19). -/
def AdmissibleStep {n : ℕ} (alpha beta : Fin n → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ i : Adjacent n, alpha (nextPosition i) ≠ alpha i.val + 1 ∧
    alpha (nextPosition i) ≠ alpha i.val - 1 ∧ beta = alpha ∘ adjacentPerm i

/-- Finite reachability by admissible swaps; never defined by endpoints (p.19). -/
def AdmissiblyEquivalent {n : ℕ} (alpha beta : Fin n → ℂ) : Prop :=
  Relation.ReflTransGen AdmissibleStep alpha beta

/-- An ordinary tableau records each successively added box. Every prefix is
a finite lower ideal, so this is exactly a path in the Young graph (pp.19–20). -/
def YoungTableau (n : ℕ) :=
  {t : Fin n → ℕ × ℕ // Function.Injective t ∧
    ∀ m : ℕ, m ≤ n → IsLowerSet {b | ∃ i : Fin n, i.val < m ∧ t i = b}}

/-- The endpoint diagram of the path (p.20). -/
def tableauShape {n : ℕ} (T : YoungTableau n) : YoungDiagram where
  cells := Finset.univ.image T.val
  isLowerSet := by
    intro b a hab hb
    have hb' : ∃ i : Fin n, i.val < n ∧ T.val i = b := by
      rcases Finset.mem_image.mp hb with ⟨i, _, hi⟩
      exact ⟨i, i.isLt, hi⟩
    rcases T.property.2 n (le_refl n) hab hb' with ⟨i, _, hi⟩
    exact Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨i, Finset.mem_univ i, hi⟩

/-- Content is column minus row in Mathlib's matrix coordinates (p.20). -/
def boxContent (b : ℕ × ℕ) : ℤ := (b.2 : ℤ) - (b.1 : ℤ)

/-- The content vector computed from the actual boxes, not from a spectrum
or an existence choice (p.20). -/
def tableauContent {n : ℕ} (T : YoungTableau n) : Fin n → ℂ :=
  fun i => (boxContent (T.val i) : ℂ)

/-- A tableau swap exchanges adjacent labels in different rows and columns
(p.20). All intermediate tableaux remain actual paths. -/
def TableauStep {n : ℕ} (T U : YoungTableau n) : Prop :=
  ∃ i : Adjacent n, (T.val i.val).1 ≠ (T.val (nextPosition i)).1 ∧
    (T.val i.val).2 ≠ (T.val (nextPosition i)).2 ∧
    U.val = T.val ∘ adjacentPerm i

/-- Lookup of a box's zero-based label in a tableau. Used only on boxes of
that tableau in inversion counts (p.21). -/
def labelAt {n : ℕ} (T : YoungTableau n) (b : ℕ × ℕ) : ℕ :=
  ∑ i : Fin n, if T.val i = b then i.val else 0

/-- The source inversion number of the relabelling from T to U, for equal
endpoints; this is not an infimum with a default value (p.21). -/
def inversionsBetween {n : ℕ} (T U : YoungTableau n) : ℕ :=
  (Finset.univ.filter (fun p : Fin n × Fin n =>
    p.1 < p.2 ∧ labelAt U (T.val p.1) > labelAt U (T.val p.2))).card

/-- The Young graph's actual one-box edges, independently of lattice covers
(p.20; p.25). -/
def YoungEdge (mu lam : YoungDiagram) : Prop :=
  mu ≤ lam ∧ (lam.cells \ mu.cells).card = 1

/-- Deleting the last symbol from its cycle, keeping all other letters.
removeNone redirects the arrow into the deleted letter to its successor (p.25). -/
def deleteLast (n : ℕ) (g : Equiv.Perm (Fin (n + 1))) : Equiv.Perm (Fin n) :=
  Equiv.removeNone ((Equiv.permCongr finSuccEquivLast) g)

/-- The linear extension of deletion, not an algebra homomorphism (p.25). -/
def deletionLinear (n : ℕ) : SymmetricAlgebra (n + 1) →ₗ[ℂ] SymmetricAlgebra n :=
  MonoidAlgebra.mapDomainLinearMap ℂ ℂ (deleteLast n)

/-- Embedding the last k letters of S_(n+k), with no rebasing of ambient
YJM elements (p.26). -/
def tailEmbedding (n k : ℕ) : Fin k ↪ Fin (n + k) where
  toFun i := ⟨n + i.val, by omega⟩
  inj' := by
    intro i j hij
    apply Fin.ext
    have hval : n + i.val = n + j.val :=
      congrArg (fun x : Fin (n + k) => x.val) hij
    exact Nat.add_left_cancel hval

/-- An individual element of the tail S_k inside the ambient algebra (p.26). -/
def tailElement (n k : ℕ) (g : Equiv.Perm (Fin k)) : SymmetricAlgebra (n + k) :=
  MonoidAlgebra.single (g.viaEmbedding (tailEmbedding n k)) 1

/-- Transitivity on all n letters: precisely a full n-cycle when n≥1,
including the identity for n=1 (p.28). -/
def IsFullCycle {n : ℕ} (g : Equiv.Perm (Fin n)) : Prop :=
  ∀ i j, ∃ r : ℕ, (g ^ r) i = j

/-- Free generators Y_1,...,Y_n and s_1,...,s_(n-1) (p.15). -/
abbrev HeckeFree (n : ℕ) := FreeAlgebra ℂ (Sum (Fin n) (Adjacent n))

/-- Free Y generator (p.15). -/
def freeY {n : ℕ} (i : Fin n) : HeckeFree n := FreeAlgebra.ι ℂ (Sum.inl i)

/-- Free Coxeter generator (p.15). -/
def freeS {n : ℕ} (i : Adjacent n) : HeckeFree n := FreeAlgebra.ι ℂ (Sum.inr i)

/-- The exact degenerate affine Hecke relations: commuting Y's, Coxeter
involutions with braid and distant relations, and s_i Y_i+1=Y_(i+1) s_i
where the added 1 is the algebra identity (pp.14–15). -/
def HeckeRelations (n : ℕ) (x y : HeckeFree n) : Prop :=
  (∃ i j : Fin n, x = freeY i * freeY j ∧ y = freeY j * freeY i) ∨
  (∃ i : Adjacent n, x = freeS i * freeS i ∧ y = 1) ∨
  (∃ i j : Adjacent n, (i.val.val + 1 < j.val.val ∨ j.val.val + 1 < i.val.val) ∧
    x = freeS i * freeS j ∧ y = freeS j * freeS i) ∨
  (∃ i j : Adjacent n, j.val.val = i.val.val + 1 ∧
    x = freeS i * freeS j * freeS i ∧ y = freeS j * freeS i * freeS j) ∨
  (∃ (i : Adjacent n) (j : Fin n), j ≠ i.val ∧ j ≠ nextPosition i ∧
    x = freeS i * freeY j ∧ y = freeY j * freeS i) ∨
  (∃ i : Adjacent n, x = freeS i * freeY i.val + 1 ∧
    y = freeY (nextPosition i) * freeS i)

/-- The presented algebra H(n); this definition does not identify it with its
finite-dimensional group-algebra image (p.15). -/
abbrev Hecke (n : ℕ) := RingQuot (HeckeRelations n)

/-- Canonical presented Y generator (p.15). -/
def heckeY {n : ℕ} (i : Fin n) : Hecke n :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom ℂ (HeckeRelations n) (freeY i)

/-- Canonical presented s generator (p.15). -/
def heckeS {n : ℕ} (i : Adjacent n) : Hecke n :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom ℂ (HeckeRelations n) (freeS i)

/-- Relation killing Y_1. At n=0 the relation is empty (p.15). -/
def KillFirst (n : ℕ) (x y : Hecke n) : Prop :=
  ∃ i : Fin n, i.val = 0 ∧ x = heckeY i ∧ y = 0

/-- Hermitian pairing in coordinates, conjugate-linear in the first input
(pp.6–7). It is not the default Pi norm. -/
def hermitianPair {d : ℕ} (H : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ)
    (v w : Fin d → ℂ) : ℂ :=
  ∑ i : Fin d, star (v i) * ∑ j : Fin d, H i j * w j

/-- The chosen positive definite invariant Hermitian inner product of p.7.
Keeping its Gram matrix explicit avoids treating the Pi norm as invariant. -/
structure InvariantHermitian {n d : ℕ}
    (rho : SymmetricAlgebra n →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ)) where
  gram : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ
  hermitian : gram.IsHermitian
  positive : ∀ v : Fin d → ℂ, v ≠ 0 → 0 < (hermitianPair gram v v).re
  invariant : ∀ (g : Equiv.Perm (Fin n)) (v w : Fin d → ℂ),
    hermitianPair gram (rho (MonoidAlgebra.single g 1) v)
      (rho (MonoidAlgebra.single g 1) w) = hermitianPair gram v w

/-- Zero has squared length zero, so it cannot be a unit basis vector. -/
example {d : ℕ} (H : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d) ℂ) : hermitianPair H 0 0 = 0 := by
  simp [hermitianPair]

/-- A concrete coordinate representative of an irreducible S_n-module (p.6).
The zero representation is excluded by IsIrreducibleAlgebra. -/
structure IrreducibleRepresentative (n : ℕ) where
  dimension : ℕ
  action : SymmetricAlgebra n →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin dimension → ℂ)
  simple : IsIrreducibleAlgebra action

/-- Actual equivalence of complex representations, not equality of dimensions
or coincidence of a selected eigenvalue (p.6). -/
def EquivalentRepresentatives {n : ℕ} (p q : IrreducibleRepresentative n) : Prop :=
  ∃ e : (Fin p.dimension → ℂ) ≃ₗ[ℂ] (Fin q.dimension → ℂ),
    ∀ a v, e (p.action a v) = q.action a (e v)

/-- Representation equivalence is an equivalence relation (p.6). -/
instance representativeSetoid (n : ℕ) : Setoid (IrreducibleRepresentative n) where
  r := EquivalentRepresentatives
  iseqv := {
    refl := fun p => ⟨LinearEquiv.refl ℂ _, by intro a v; rfl⟩
    symm := by
      intro p q h
      rcases h with ⟨e, he⟩
      refine ⟨e.symm, ?_⟩
      intro a v
      apply e.injective
      simpa using (he a (e.symm v)).symm
    trans := by
      intro p q r h k
      rcases h with ⟨e, he⟩
      rcases k with ⟨f, hf⟩
      refine ⟨e.trans f, ?_⟩
      intro a v
      change f (e (p.action a v)) = r.action a (f (e v))
      rw [he, hf] }

/-- A set-sized skeleton: genuine equivalence classes of all irreducibles,
constructed independently of Young diagrams (p.6). -/
abbrev IrreducibleClass (n : ℕ) := Quotient (representativeSetoid n)

/-- A representative of a genuine equivalence class; no desired spectral or
branching property is used to choose it (pp.6–7). -/
def classRepresentative {n : ℕ} (C : IrreducibleClass n) : IrreducibleRepresentative n :=
  Quotient.out C

/-- Actual adjacent restriction multiplicity between irreducible classes (p.6). -/
def branchingMultiplicity {n : ℕ} (C : IrreducibleClass n) (D : IrreducibleClass (n + 1)) : ℕ :=
  Module.finrank ℂ (intertwiningSpace
    ((classRepresentative D).action.comp (prefixInclusion (Nat.le_succ n)))
    (classRepresentative C).action)

/-- Paths in the actual branching graph, independently of tableaux (pp.6–7).
At level zero the irreducible of the scalar algebra is the trivial vertex. -/
structure BranchingPath (n : ℕ) where
  vertex : (i : Fin (n + 1)) → IrreducibleClass i.val
  edge : ∀ i : Fin n, 0 < branchingMultiplicity
    (vertex ⟨i.val, by omega⟩) (vertex ⟨i.val + 1, by omega⟩)

/-- Paths ending at the specified actual irreducible class (p.7). -/
def BranchingPathsToClass {n : ℕ} (C : IrreducibleClass n) :=
  {T : BranchingPath n // T.vertex (Fin.last n) = C}

/-- The C-isotypic subspace of a restricted target module is the sum of ranges
of all actual equivariant maps from C (p.7). Submodule suprema are genuine
sums of subspaces, with no unbounded-real default convention. -/
def restrictedIsotypic {n d : ℕ}
    (rho : SymmetricAlgebra n →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ))
    (i : Fin (n + 1)) (C : IrreducibleClass i.val) : Submodule ℂ (Fin d → ℂ) :=
  ⨆ f : intertwiningSpace
    (rho.comp (prefixInclusion (by omega : i.val ≤ n))) (classRepresentative C).action,
    LinearMap.range f.val

/-- The canonical path subspace: intersect the independently constructed
isotypic subspaces along the path (p.7). No line dimension, decomposition,
eigenbasis or diagonal-algebra equality is assumed in this definition. -/
def canonicalLine {n : ℕ} (C : IrreducibleClass n) (T : BranchingPath n) :
    Submodule ℂ (Fin (classRepresentative C).dimension → ℂ) :=
  ⨅ i : Fin (n + 1), restrictedIsotypic (classRepresentative C).action i (T.vertex i)

/-- Actual weights in a particular class, independent of the diagram label
and all admissible-swap relations (p.13). -/
def ClassHasWeight {n : ℕ} (C : IrreducibleClass n) (alpha : Fin n → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∃ v, IsWeightVector (classRepresentative C).action alpha v

/-- A path's weight has the prescribed prefix weight in each actual vertex
representation (pp.7,13). This avoids choosing eigenvalues by a default value. -/
def PathHasWeight {n : ℕ} (T : BranchingPath n) (alpha : Fin n → ℂ) : Prop :=
  ∀ i : Fin (n + 1), ClassHasWeight (T.vertex i)
    (fun j : Fin i.val => alpha ⟨j.val, by omega⟩)

/-- Genuine maximal commutativity, including ambient containment, rather than
commutativity alone (pp.8,13). -/
def IsMaximalCommutative {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A]
    (B : Subalgebra ℂ A) : Prop :=
  IsCommutativeSubalgebra B ∧ ∀ D : Subalgebra ℂ A,
    B ≤ D → IsCommutativeSubalgebra D → D = B

/-- Coordinate representatives are equivalent to themselves. -/
example {n : ℕ} (p : IrreducibleRepresentative n) : EquivalentRepresentatives p p :=
  ⟨LinearEquiv.refl ℂ _, by intro a v; rfl⟩

/-- Last-letter inclusions retain the index on old letters. -/
example {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n) (i : Fin m) : (prefixEmbedding h i).val = i.val := rfl

/-- Small YJM normalization: X_1 is zero at every positive level. -/
example (n : ℕ) : yjm (⟨0, Nat.zero_lt_succ n⟩ : Fin (n + 1)) = 0 := by
  simp [yjm]

/-- The zero-dimensional algebra module is explicitly excluded. -/
example {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A]
    (rho : A →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin 0 → ℂ)) : ¬ IsIrreducibleAlgebra rho := by
  simp [IsIrreducibleAlgebra]

/-- No zero vector is admitted into the spectral definition. -/
example {n d : ℕ} (rho : SymmetricAlgebra n →ₐ[ℂ] Module.End ℂ (Fin d → ℂ))
    (alpha : Fin n → ℂ) : ¬ IsWeightVector rho alpha 0 := by
  simp [IsWeightVector]

/-- Empty content vector is valid, as required by the trivial S_0 case. -/
example : (fun i : Fin 0 => Fin.elim0 i) ∈ contentVectors 0 := by
  simp [contentVectors]

/-- One row step gives content +1, while one column step gives -1. -/
example : boxContent (0, 1) = 1 ∧ boxContent (1, 0) = -1 := by
  norm_num [boxContent]

/-- Finite reachability includes the length-zero swap sequence. -/
example {n : ℕ} (alpha : Fin n → ℂ) : AdmissiblyEquivalent alpha alpha :=
  Relation.ReflTransGen.refl

/-- Tail inclusion acts on the actual last letters. -/
example (n k : ℕ) (i : Fin k) : (tailEmbedding n k i).val = n + i.val := rfl

/-- Each presented Coxeter generator is an involution by its defining relation. -/
example {n : ℕ} (i : Adjacent n) : heckeS i * heckeS i = 1 := by
  have h := RingQuot.mkAlgHom_rel ℂ (s := HeckeRelations n)
    (Or.inr (Or.inl ⟨i, rfl, rfl⟩))
  simpa [heckeS] using h

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Renew46.P26


